NOTE ON SCOPE

This MIT licence covers the SOFTWARE in this repository: everything outside the
`content/` directory.

The LESSON CONTENT in `content/` is licensed separately under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International. See LICENSE-CONTENT.

Why the split, in short: the code is infrastructure and should spread with as
little friction as possible, including inside companies. The curriculum is a
commons built from many people's unpaid hours, and share-alike keeps it one —
it can be copied, translated and built upon, but not enclosed. CONTRIBUTING.md
explains the reasoning at greater length.
